{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons","id":679302,"title":"The Yankee and the Allied pantheons.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-26T13:40:18-07:00","id":679302,"title":"The Yankee and the Allied pantheons.","content":"I have for a long time thought it was a shame these two pantheons did not get a proper Titan War write up. I consider them both to be an excellent representation of the other half of the american gods meet exalted thing that scion is going for. They are the ideals and values that mythological gods used to reflect in their time. That and i also because i am uncreative fucktwat beseech you all to help me ponder up guide, creature, relic and follower ideas from 1-5 for these pantheons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T10:46:17-08:00","id":770831,"title":"","content":"I like these Pantheons, however most of the boards hate them with a blind passion. I wouldn't mind seeing them get further details in a supplement, including notes on there history before and after WWII.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T20:29:30-08:00","id":771182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=770831#post770831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like these Pantheons, however most of the boards hate them with a blind passion. I wouldn't mind seeing them get further details in a supplement, including notes on there history before and after WWII.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, the word &quot;Yankee&quot; doesn't sound right to me, since that was a word used by the South during the revolution to refer to abolitionists and we don't even use the word in modern dialect anymore, unless we're doing a mocking impersonation of the Confederates. It doesn't really sound like a proper pantheon name for America. I also think The Allied pantheon should have also been expanded beyond just 3 people from each region.<br /> <br /> The major problem with the Yankee and Allied is I have no idea who many of these people are.<br /> <br /> The only ones I recognize are Paul Bunyan, Pecos Bill (by name), Betsy Ross, Br'er Rabbit, John Henry, Uncle Sam (by name), Johnny Appleseed, Baba Yaga, Robin Hood.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Madam Guillotine, John Bull, Marianne, Rodina Mat, Rossie the Riveter, The Citizen, D'Artagnan,Britanna, and Columbia, I have no idea who they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:11:26-08:00","id":771227,"title":"","content":"I'd like a write up for their god realms<br /> <br /> A reason for the Hatred for them is some of the figures, seem almost farcical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T04:12:39-08:00","id":771377,"title":"","content":"While not too fond of the Yanke, I remember writing down an Overworld for them once. I'll look over my notes to see if I can find them. Might take a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T04:25:50-08:00","id":771386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=771227#post771227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a write up for their god realms<br /> <br /> A reason for the Hatred for them is some of the figures, seem almost farcical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well their purview focuses on the human spirit, inspiring hard work and dedication to overcome the impossible. Plus it's tier 10 Boon is to just drop a nuke on the Titans.<br /> <br /> I could see the Overworld reflecting a city reminiscent of the industrial revolution, constantly improving itself throughout the application of new ideas and trades.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for them being farcical, they're taken from American folklore. Paul Bunyan, Pecos Bill and Johnny Appleseed were actually popular when I was growing up. Not too sure how well received they'd be today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-22-2015, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T06:39:46-08:00","id":771451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=771182#post771182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Madam Guillotine, John Bull, Marianne, Rodina Mat, Rossie the Riveter, The Citizen, D'Artagnan,Britanna, and Columbia, I have no idea who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> John Bull was the British version of Uncle Sam, a personification of the nation. <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/John_Bull_-_World_War_I_recruiting_poster.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a picture</a> of him in a similar pose to the ubiquitous &quot;Uncle Sam Wants You&quot; poster. There's a number of images showing Sam and John <a href=\"http://www.loc.gov/exhibits/british/images/75avc.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">working together</a>, particularly during WWII.<br /> <br /> Rosie the Riveter was the title of <a href=\"http://www.militarytrader.com/wp-content/uploads/il_fullxfull.508201205_1gbw.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this piece</a> by Normal Rockwell, showing a woman in a then-unfamiliar context: doing &quot;man's&quot; work. While the men were mostly in Europe during the war, many women went to work in various industries keeping the war machine turning. The name is also often applied to the <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/12/We_Can_Do_It%21.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">We Can Do It!</a> propaganda poster. It's a separate woman, but the sentiment is the same.<br /> <br /> D'Artagnan was a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Batz-Castelmore_d%27Artagnan\" target=\"_blank\">real guy</a>, fictionalized as the &quot;fourth Musketeer&quot; in the <i>Three Musketeers</i> series alongside Athos, Porthos, and Aramis.<br /> <br /> Britannia and Columbia are, like John Bull and Uncle Sam, the female personifications of the nations of the UK and America. Britannia's seen throughout the pages of the <i>League of Extraordinary Gentlemen</i>, for example. Washington, D.C., the <i>District of Columbia</i> is named after this Columbia. Likewise the floating city of Columbia from Bioshock: Infinite. Columbia's been largely replaced by Lady Liberty in the public eye these days.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.sonofthesouth.net/uncle-sam/images/uncle-sam-john-bull-poster.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a poster</a> of Uncle Sam and John Bull shaking hands, overseen by Columbia and Britannia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T06:48:23-08:00","id":771452,"title":"","content":"To add to that: Meeting Madame Guillotine was an euphemism for being beheaded by the Guillotine during the French Revolution. So shes not as much a historic figure as she is the personification of what the French Revolution was about<b></b>: Rooting out any and all men and women who stood against the Revolution and its ideals, potentially leading to tyrants like Robespierre but also doing what is cruel, but necessary. There also was a movie in the 30s of the same name which was about a revolotionary and a nobleman falling in love, if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T07:27:39-08:00","id":771468,"title":"","content":"Ah, you'd think being descended from the French aristocracy, I'd have known more about her. Actually, I do remember hearing something about Madame Guillotine a long time ago on the history channel. Don't remember anything specific about her, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T10:36:05-08:00","id":771586,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a Yankee Pantheon if not necessarily the members of it...someone had mentioned once doing it as &quot;Rome Reborn&quot; and while I liked parts of that idea (Uncle Sam=Caesar=Roman Emperor as a God) it didn't necessarily fit. So I picked and chose gods from other pantheons not currently being used in the books and said they &quot;immigrated&quot; and found their own places (so Anansi instead of &quot;Br'er Rabbit&quot; and so on) and said the pantheon's (such as it is) main difficulty is agreeing on anything since there really isn't a classic hierarchy among them.<br /> <br /> Of course, I also said that the reason they could get away with this is that the Titan of Metal had lain waste to the &quot;Native Pantheon&quot; and threatened to run rampant unless someone stopped it...the Yankee Pantheon is what we got.<br /> <br /> The Titan of Metal, such as it is was born from an American Literature class. The American Industrial revolution left a rather nasty scar on the psyche of the traditional descended-from-people-who-thought-European-religion-wasn't-hard-enough folk and there was a period in literature where overall image was a person being fed to a machine and being ground up by the gears of progress. I liked that idea as an adversary, and there wasn't a Metal Titan yet, so here we go. Unfortunately it deals mostly with fears found in the modern age (the drudgery of work, big brother watching, you're a cog in the wheel of life and nothing more, etc...) so there really isn't any specific bad guy gods I could use there...of course &quot;WE ARE THE BORG&quot; is a thing, so maybe that general aesthetic might be for the best.<br /> <br /> For the record I also changed the Pantheon Specific Purview of the Yankees (Industry is too good as a general crafting boons to not use there) and shifted focus to <i>dreams</i>. Specifically the realizing of them. America was built by people with dreams and the drive to see them through. So the actual battle of the pantheon isn't tradition vs progress, it's optimism versus pessimism. Are we going to take a stand and be the good people we set out to be? Or is the inevitable weight of reality going to crush us all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I'M SORRY, I CAN'T HEAR YOU OVER THE SOUND OF HOW MANY MALFEAS CHARMS I HAVE!!!</b><i>~King Crazy Genius</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/345-kandagger","name":"Kandagger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T16:00:12-08:00","id":771796,"title":"","content":"What do you mean? You have a perfectly legit form of Titanspawn, The Paparazzi of modern media. What better way to destroy a Scion's legend than to humiliate and discredit them in front of thousands of witnesses via broadcast?<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The captain of the varsity foot ball team is wanted for questioning in regards to the murder of [insert name] the president and CEO of [insert company]. The suspect was seen fleeing the victim's private residence shortly before it exploded into flames!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-22-2015, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T16:47:46-08:00","id":771873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=770831#post770831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like these Pantheons, however most of the boards hate them with a blind passion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing blind about it. That said: when they get around to the rules and guidelines for how to establish a new Pantheon, I would not be averse to something like the Yankees being used as an example. Assuming that the likes of Uncle Sam, Columbia, John Henry, and Paul Bunyan are viable Mantles, I could see a group of immigrant Scions assuming them during a time of great crisis (such as World War II) as a means of helping rally the troops, as it were. A key difference is that every member of this synthetic Pantheon would have had a life before its establishment. <br /> <br /> The Allied Pantheon, OTOH, I have no interest in whatsoever. Separate British, French, and Russian National Pantheons, <i>maybe</i>; though unlike the United States, these nations have long histories and associated mythologies, and I'd rather <b>Scion</b> focus on those instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T18:24:45-08:00","id":771958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=771227#post771227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a write up for their god realms<br /> <br /> A reason for the Hatred for them is some of the figures, seem almost farcical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost? You're being too nice. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The main problem with them is that, with Scion's pretty strong and clear mythologic bent, they overall make for a very bad fit indeed for actual deities of their own with a pantheon and stuff. Not that it's all useless or badwrongfun, but their delivery strays too far from the rest of the setting not to be contentious.<br /> The fact some are straight out of literature or (propaganda) art instead of any actual myths or legends doesn't help any.<br /> <br /> That said, there are some pretty viable NPCs there if one only takes the time to rehash and tweak things - in my own games, &quot;Uncle Sam&quot; was an escaped and somewhat amnesiac Zeus adopting a disguise and allies to oppose Caligula and the divine conspirators behind his usurpation, Columbia, Britannia &amp; Marianne were disguises of Athena, the actual strategic brains coordinating the &quot;Allied Pantheons&quot; as a smokescreen to distract and foil the demented scheme of the Axis-connected pantheons. Some i turned into scions like John Henry &amp; Rosie the Rivetter (Hephaestus or Wayland Smith), Pecos Bill (Br'er Rabbit), Robin Hood &amp; D'artganan (sires unknown) and others as gods of many origins (Br'er Rabbit as Coyote, Bunyan a giant of unspecified origin, Appleseed as a wandering Tammuz in disguise, Rodina Mat as an unamed rogue vanir goddess, etc).<br /> <br /> Largest change i did was with Madame Guillotine and the Citizen, who in my game become the avatars of a mostly unknown titan connected to fate, order, tiranny, abuse of power and nightmarish states straight out of Orwell &amp; Kafka and, as you can guess, a major antagonist in the backstory of my own games. Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-12-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T06:01:11-08:00","id":772257,"title":"","content":"Oh curious... if the Axis won, what would likely happen to the Yankee Pantheon Mass beheadings? Or be forced to vow fealty to their conquerers.<br /> <br /> The thought of Uncle Sam b eing forced to bend knee to Amateratsu... really tickles my fancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T09:29:36-08:00","id":772370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=772257#post772257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh curious... if the Axis won, what would likely happen to the Yankee Pantheon Mass beheadings? Or be forced to vow fealty to their conquerers.<br /> <br /> The thought of Uncle Sam b eing forced to bend knee to Amateratsu... really tickles my fancy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't think it would effect the gods all that much. America won the war, yet the Amatsukami are still going strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:35:38-08:00","id":772495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=771182#post771182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we don't even use the word in modern dialect anymore, unless we're doing a mocking impersonation of the Confederates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe damnyankees don't, but it's still pretty common parlance in (apparently parts of) the South.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 11-24-2015, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T14:05:55-08:00","id":772514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=772495#post772495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe damnyankees like you don't, but it's still pretty common parlance in the South.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm from Georgia, which I think was part of the confederates. I don't know, I slept through History.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:31:17-08:00","id":772616,"title":"","content":"am oklahoman.<br /> <br /> then again... Before I came down with MS I was hoping to expatriate... so not a typical example of the culture out here in the bible belt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T19:37:32-08:00","id":772734,"title":"","content":"To hear my grandmother tell it. Yankees come, spend their money, and leave. A Damn Yankee comes and stays. She was married to my grandfather for years and they still called her that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 11-23-2015, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T19:57:22-08:00","id":772747,"title":"","content":"Huh, weird, maybe Georgians are just more civilized <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Still the point stands that the pantheon is using a name that originated with the people who opposed and vilified them, not the actual supporters of the Scions in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:30:35-08:00","id":774931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=772495#post772495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe damnyankees don't, but it's still pretty common parlance in (apparently parts of) the South.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm from St. Petersburg, Florida. We don't use the word Yankee. That said, Central Florida is much more cosmopolitan than \u200bNorth Florida, A.K.A. the Redneck Riviera. For those who don't know, Florida is kind of a microcosm of American politics, only upside down; the further South you get in Florida, the more Liberal. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T19:58:04-08:00","id":775751,"title":"","content":"&quot;Liberal FL&quot; is like a belt across the middle. SW Florida is about as conservative a place as there is anywhere in the US.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T19:15:39-08:00","id":783852,"title":"","content":"Miami is FULL of retired New Yorkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T12:01:30-08:00","id":787540,"title":"","content":"Oh curious On Treacherous Allied Pantheon members (Notably those of Madam Gullotine) Is starting a new dynasty a reasonable goal? <br /> <br /> I could just see a new Czar or king of france emerge...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T17:02:02-08:00","id":787717,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it would be a very reasonable one. Since I think it mentions them having suffered enormous loses to the Axis pantheon. So trying to rebuild their power structure makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:22:35-08:00","id":835029,"title":"","content":"Do remember that Britannia herself is a real goddess that was worshiped after the Romans conquered the British Isles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:45:30-08:00","id":837929,"title":"","content":"I never liked the modern national pantheons as written. My idea instead was to just have a Demigod-level coalition of Scions from various Pantheons representing American folks heroes (playing up the melting pot), with Athena and her allies backing Western Democracy since the Classical resurgence of the Enlightenment as the little project she's been tinkering with since Athens didn't work out. She is called Columbia, Britannia, and Marianne in her modern guises.<br /> <br /> I my take on WW 2, Olympus split in half like they did over Troy. Allied with Athena (inspired by &quot;the Apotheosis of Washington&quot;) are Hermes (commerce), Hephaestus (industry), Poseidon (sea power), Demeter (agriculture), and Dionysus (counter-culture).<br /> <br /> The &quot;we want a new Roman Empire faction&quot; are Venus, Mars, Juno, Vesta, Apollo, and Diana. In addition to Quirinus of course though he doesn't get a vote on Olympus. Janus being Janus played at supporting the &quot;Roman&quot; faction but was really backing the anti-Mussolini Italian resistance. Two-faced bastard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Zeus and Hades remain neutral as they always do in mortal wars.<br /> <br /> But as for the American Folkheroes, Pecos Bill is a Tornado riding Scion of Zeus, Harriet Tubman drew (through Christianity) on a lineage going back to Eshu-Elegba opening ways, Rosie the Riveter is a daughter of Brighid, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-27-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T09:20:33-08:00","id":838085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=837929#post837929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I my take on WW 2, Olympus split in half like they did over Troy. Allied with Athena (inspired by &quot;the Apotheosis of Washington&quot;) are Hermes (commerce), Hephaestus (industry), Poseidon (sea power), Demeter (agriculture), and Dionysus (counter-culture).<br /> <br /> The &quot;we want a new Roman Empire faction&quot; are Venus, Mars, Juno, Vesta, Apollo, and Diana. In addition to Quirinus of course though he doesn't get a vote on Olympus. Janus being Janus played at supporting the &quot;Roman&quot; faction but was really backing the anti-Mussolini Italian resistance. Two-faced bastard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just can't see Juno EVER allying with the Apollo &amp; Diana (and possibly Venus, but also possilby not) considering they were the bastard children of her cheating husband. Reasoning that she veered off this course during the Trojan War due to her desire to punish Paris for his decision on the Golden Apple. (Besides, Athena could be regarded as the child of Zeus <i>sua sponte</i> without involving of cheating, And Hermes, as an effective &quot;servant&quot; might be okay. That's the sort of thing one does with unfortunate bastard sons.)<br /> <br /> Sure, Mars, abso-effing-lutely. And maybe Venus as his lawful wife? <br /> <br /> I would change Poseidon over to the Roman side (the Neptune/Njord Alliance?), especially considering that Neptune explicitly had dominion over the Ocean Sea as part of his &quot;inheritance&quot; from getting the realms of Oceanus &amp; Tethys). Until that dominance was thwarted by Athena's (with Hermes' input?) little Bletchley Park thing turning the tables (or tide?). (In the Eastern theater, it wasn't really naval dominance that really won the war in any meaningful way. It was being able to out-think the naval dominance to open up the supply lines.)<br /> <br /> Vesta/Hestia would probably sit it out with Pluto/Hades and Jupiter/Zeus. Since that's what she does. (Like she did during the Trojan War). <br /> <br /> Bacchus/Dionysius perhaps as another two-faced, undependable, slippery joiner/non-joiner depending on his whims and whatever side was currently making the whole thing more of a farce or tragedy. Counter-culture, such as it was, wasn't really something the Allies supported much more than the Axis. Conformity is pretty much dogma in militarized societies and that was both sides during the war. <br /> <br /> It seems kinda sad that Hephaestus has almost nothing to do with innovation. Especially since the Norse gods smith god is mostly a cipher (Volund, about whom myths are mostly quiet - possibly indicating an Aesir alliance with the dvergar?). Really Hephaestus would have been more in charge of getting America's massive resource advantage into play. Not so much the &quot;god of cool new stuff&quot; (which the Nazi's had in spades, despite their overall anti-science stances) as the &quot;god of assembly lines&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T10:20:31-08:00","id":838126,"title":"","content":"<b><u>This was originally posted by Telgar on the old forums.</u><br /> <br /> Betsy Ross \u2013 Immortal Woman (Guide 2)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Remembered now for sewing the first American Flag in 1776, Betsy Ross was otherwise an unassuming woman. Now historians doubt that she even performed the single deed that garnered her fame. True or not, Miss Betsy Ross gained the attention of one of the few Scions walking the World in the 18th century. She was a hard worker and she survived a life full of many trials. Something about her spurred the Scion to grant her a gift. Ross is blind, old and fragile, but she is most certainly alive. She has almost three hundred years of experience and knowledge to bestow on young Scions, though her viewpoints are a little old fashioned.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Br\u2019er Rabbit \u2013 Trickster Avatar</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">No one is sure exactly who Br\u2019er Rabbit is, because there are many Br\u2019er Rabbits. The name and form of the old Southern trickster are worn by many different Gods dropping by the Deep South for a visit. Sometimes he is a regular hare that acts in extraordinary ways, other times he is an anthropomorphic rabbit who walks about upright, wearing trousers and a collared shirt. He\u2019s even appeared as an old country man with buck teeth, a harelip and too-big ears. Some suspects for Br\u2019er Rabbit include Coyote, Anansi and even Loki. Most commonly he is assumed to be either a West African or a Native American deity assuming a more modern guise. Sometimes Br\u2019er Rabbit helps Scions, but he\u2019s just as likely to be stirring up the trouble that has drawn Scions to the area in the first place. You just never know.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Columbia \u2013 Minor Goddess (Guide 4)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">There are conflicting tales of Columbia\u2019s origin and she isn\u2019t clearing them up. Some say she is a daughter of Athena, others say she is an Avatar or aspect of the older Goddess, still others suggest that Columbia is a Titanspawn, possibly a creature of Logos, somehow related to Themis. Whatever her true origin, Columbia presents herself as the Goddess of the United States. She has little respect from more established figures and, in truth, has little power of her own. She has no Scions and, so far as anyone can tell, never has had any. She does take an interest in any Scion who meddles too closely in the affairs of the United States and sometimes appears to guide them onto the \u2018correct\u2019 course for her favored nation. Since the 20\u2019s, Columbia has more and more often appeared as Lady Liberty, often carrying a torch and wearing robes and a crown resembling those on a certain famous copper statue. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>John Henry \u2013 Ghost, Former Scion of Heracles (Guide 2)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Remembered in story and song, John Henry would have been a great Scion if he hadn\u2019t worked himself to death in the earliest stages of his Legend. He is now a ghost and since the breaking of Tartarus, has returned to the World and finds much to his distaste. Too much automation, too much laziness and reliance on machines and mass production instead of hard work and quality. He still has knowledge of strange and Legendary World that Scions inhabit to offer, as well as his own experience.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Johnny Appleseed \u2013 Adopted Legendary Persona (Guide 2)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The real Johnny Appleseed, John Chapman, was an extraordinary mortal man who lived a life that earned him some measure of Legendary status, but in 1845 he died, as mortals do. Chapman had so impressed some of the lesser Immortals and nature spirits of North America that they continue his Legend. Johnny Appleseed appears here and there, a form worn by a variety of nature spirits native to the United States, especially in Pennsylvania, Ohio, Indiana and Illinois. He tends forests, protects animals and encourages preservation. Scions who are attempting to protect nature and its creatures in the areas he frequents can sometimes find Johnny Appleseed and ask for his help. He may even take an extended interest in preservation-inclined Scions in his ranges.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Paul Bunyan \u2013 Earth Giant (Guide 3)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Now known as the archetypical lumberjack, Bunyan\u2019s history goes back much, much further. It goes all the way back to Vinland, where Paul Bunyan was simply a Giant who pursued a Norse Scion across the ocean. The Scion slipped through his grasp, but their fight forced the young Hero to abandon his favorite mount: a blue ox. The ox was taken by Bunyan as a trophy of his victory and became his constant companion. Over time, he acclimated to his home in the New World and grew to care greatly for the earth and forests of Canada and the northern United States. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Pecos Bill \u2013 Demigod (Guide 2-3)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">A brash Scion from the American West, Pecos Bill\u2019s deeds were enough to earn him the status of Demigod, but never to propel him towards Apotheosis. As the wild west was tamed, Bill slowly withdrew from the World more and more, spending time in several of the Terra Incognitae scattered through the West. Pecos Bill claims to not know who his father was and there are various suspicions cast on figures such as Coyote, Thor, Zeus, Apollo and even Vayu. He still appears sometimes, often drawn out of his adventures in other Worlds by news of Titanspawn causing trouble in his old stomping grounds. He sometimes acts as a Guide for young Heroes, but he always wanders and his attention can be fleeting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Rosie the Riveter \u2013 Avatar of Brigit</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Following along with the Irish immigrants to the United States, the Goddess of Flame and Forge came to America and took on a new persona during the Second World War. She became an icon of female power and industrial might. She worked tirelessly to help uplift and empower female workers and inspire bravery and courage in all the descendants of her people, both at home and on the battlefield.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Uncle Sam \u2013 Avatar of Zeus</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The personification of the US government sometimes comes to life and walks the World, encouraging and directing the United States towards greatness. He has another name, one far more famous: Zeus. The King of the Greek Gods was all too pleased with the attention lavished upon the culture he oversaw by the fledgeling nation across the oceans. Sometimes he takes on this identity and connects with the New World in a way slightly more effective than togas and laurels.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Britannia \u2013 Minor Goddess (Guide 4) </b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Once a Scion of Minerva, Britannia was the Goddess of a faraway land that her Empire had set its eyes upon. She embraced the society that she patronized and as Roman influence in England waned, Britannia grew closer to her worshippers and farther away from her divine relatives. She has forged close ties with the native Gods of the British Isles, though she is always a foreigner among them. If young Scions wish her guidance and aid, they must only make clear that they have the best interests of England at heart.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>John Bull \u2013 Hero (Guide 2)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The only known Scion of Britannia, John Bull represents not England as a whole, but the middle class, common sense, salt of the earth people. He has walked among them for decades, locked forever in the form of a portly man just past the prime of life but with many years ahead. He reminds the people of tradition and stability during times of tumult and serves as a beacon of national identity that people can relate to, rather than sharing the remoteness that his mother and other, similar goddesses have about them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Robin Hood \u2013 Demigod (Guide 3)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The Scion most recently known as Robin Hood has worn many faces through history. He has been the Green Knight of Arthurian tales and Herne the Hunter who roamed the forests of England. Some claim that he has only played these parts occasionally and that others contributed to the legends. Cernunnos has been suspected of lending to the tale of Herne, but Robin Hood and the Horned God have always been on good terms. It may be that Cernunnos is Robin\u2019s father, but neither is inclined to discuss the matter.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>d\u2019Artagnan \u2013 Legendary Ghost (Guide 2)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Though he may not know it any longer, d'Artagnan is not the character of fiction created by Alexandre Dumas. He began life as a mortal who became captain of the Musketeers under Louis XIV. His deeds inspired Dumas\u2019 stories and the confused spirit has been captured by the webs of Legend woven around him. He has gone insane under the pressure of Fatebonds, not having the innate resistance to their shaping that true Legendary beings do. He is no longer certain if he was ever alive, and truly believes himself to be the character of Dumas\u2019 stories. While insane, he can offer guidance in certain matters to Scions willing and able to deal with his dementia.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Madame Guillotine \u2013 Avatar of Andarta</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The bloodthirsty Gaulish Goddess of War returned to France during the Revolution and enjoyed the offerings of blood and severed heads. She walked among the French under the guise of Madame Guillotine. Occasionally Andarta still takes on the form of La Terreur, but only rarely. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Marianne \u2013 Demigoddess (Guide 3)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">One of the last Scions of Teutates, Marianne rose from a long-lived Hero to a powerful Demigoddess during the turmoil of the French Revolution. She is one of the few connections between the modern nation of France and its ancient Gaulish heritage and that connection is thin indeed. Marianne fully embraces the modern world and her Gaulish family questions her loyalties. Undaunted, the brave Demigoddess seeks to always support and protect her people and her country.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Baba Yaga \u2013 Lesser Immortal (Guide 5)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The Little Grandmother of Slavic Folklore is not a Goddess, though she is more powerful than some. She lives in the Dark Forest, in a hut with no door and giant chicken legs that allow it to walk around. Gifts of blue roses can appease her, as can proper manners and heroic deeds. She exacts a great price for her aid, but she is said to know almost everything and she is one of the most powerful sorceresses in Europe.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Citizen \u2013 Legendary Ghost (Guide 2)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Once, the Citizen had a name but he no longer does. He died during the Russian Revolution but his death was of no consequence to his mission. He still defends Russia from her enemies. Disembodied and deceased, the ghost\u2019s pure strength of will has allowed him to possess the bodies of mortal Russian soldiers. He has engaged in every conflict Russia has been involved in since his death, fighting bravely and without fear of death. After all, he is already dead and it is the duty of a soldier to lay down his life for his country.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Rodina Mat \u2013 Scion of Mokosh (Guide 3)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Daughter of the ancient Slavic Earth Goddess, Rodina Mat (called Mother Russia in English) has abandoned her mortal name and assumed the role of patron for all the Russian people. She encourages fertility of the land, health of the people and distributes fortune and wealth where appropriate. Like other nationalistic figures, she will offer her aid to those who act in the best interests of the nation she favors. Unlike Columbia or Britannia, Rodina Mat is too young to have become a Goddess; she is still a Demigoddess, though one of age and power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Caligula \u2013 Titan-Sworn Scion</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">A tyrant during his rule, Caligula was sadistic and capricious. He outraged his father, Jupiter and was cut off from contact with his divine family. Spitefully, the disgraced Scion turned to the Titans and pledged himself to their service. His assassination was faked to remove him from the notice of the Roman Gods. In the pits of Tartarus, he gained dark power and now serves the Titans\u2019 purposes by taking on the role of a Guide to young Greek and Roman Scions, leading them slowly down the path of corruption he himself followed centuries ago.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Quirinus \u2013 Minor God (Guide 5)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Originally a Scion of Mars under the name Remus, the founder of Rome reached Godhood after establishing the foundations of an Empire that would shape the history of the World. He became a figure of civil order and martial prowess. He still lives on Olympus with the other Roman Gods, occasionally mentoring Scions and watching over the descendants of the people he lead to greatness.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:07:38-08:00","id":838162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=838085#post838085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just can't see Juno EVER allying with the Apollo &amp; Diana (and possibly Venus, but also possilby not) considering they were the bastard children of her cheating husband. Reasoning that she veered off this course during the Trojan War due to her desire to punish Paris for his decision on the Golden Apple. (Besides, Athena could be regarded as the child of Zeus <i>sua sponte</i> without involving of cheating, And Hermes, as an effective &quot;servant&quot; might be okay. That's the sort of thing one does with unfortunate bastard sons.)<br /> <br /> Sure, Mars, abso-effing-lutely. And maybe Venus as his lawful wife? <br /> <br /> I would change Poseidon over to the Roman side (the Neptune/Njord Alliance?), especially considering that Neptune explicitly had dominion over the Ocean Sea as part of his &quot;inheritance&quot; from getting the realms of Oceanus &amp; Tethys). Until that dominance was thwarted by Athena's (with Hermes' input?) little Bletchley Park thing turning the tables (or tide?). (In the Eastern theater, it wasn't really naval dominance that really won the war in any meaningful way. It was being able to out-think the naval dominance to open up the supply lines.)<br /> <br /> Vesta/Hestia would probably sit it out with Pluto/Hades and Jupiter/Zeus. Since that's what she does. (Like she did during the Trojan War). <br /> <br /> Bacchus/Dionysius perhaps as another two-faced, undependable, slippery joiner/non-joiner depending on his whims and whatever side was currently making the whole thing more of a farce or tragedy. Counter-culture, such as it was, wasn't really something the Allies supported much more than the Axis. Conformity is pretty much dogma in militarized societies and that was both sides during the war. <br /> <br /> It seems kinda sad that Hephaestus has almost nothing to do with innovation. Especially since the Norse gods smith god is mostly a cipher (Volund, about whom myths are mostly quiet - possibly indicating an Aesir alliance with the dvergar?). Really Hephaestus would have been more in charge of getting America's massive resource advantage into play. Not so much the &quot;god of cool new stuff&quot; (which the Nazi's had in spades, despite their overall anti-science stances) as the &quot;god of assembly lines&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Venus is not Mars' lawful wife, she's his loveR. More importantly, she's the patron goddess of Rome by way of Aeneas and the Julian Dynasty!<br /> <br /> Neptune was never of great importance to Rome comparatively. And Italian sea power is a joke.<br /> <br /> There are bastard children of Zeus on both sides, so that conflict is unavoidable. What matters though is how important Rome was to Juno. All the gods on that team are ones of special importance relative to the others in the Roman religion.<br /> <br /> The &quot;counter-culture&quot; reference was just adding Dionysus to the patronage pattern of the famous &quot;Apotheosis of Washington&quot; mural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T13:38:19-08:00","id":838199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=838162#post838162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Venus is not Mars' lawful wife, she's his loveR. More importantly, she's the patron goddess of Rome by way of Aeneas and the Julian Dynasty!<br /> <br /> Neptune was never of great importance to Rome comparatively. And Italian sea power is a joke.<br /> <br /> There are bastard children of Zeus on both sides, so that conflict is unavoidable. What matters though is how important Rome was to Juno. All the gods on that team are ones of special importance relative to the others in the Roman religion.<br /> <br /> The &quot;counter-culture&quot; reference was just adding Dionysus to the patronage pattern of the famous &quot;Apotheosis of Washington&quot; mural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah.... errr..... my bad. You are correct. Aphrodite was cheating on Hephaestus (Nods to the weaver)<br /> <br /> And the Aeneas thing trumps pretty much everything else in the &quot;Rome&quot; thing. Though the &quot;Aeneas&quot; thing was mostly Caesar pushing his agenda and getting some serious help on the literary front.... The Remus/Romulus &amp; Mars story is much much older and intrinsic. But that only solidifies the Mars/Venus role in the cabal. Plus, Mars would probably want her along, and she would probably do it in a locked negative homeostatic feedback loop with her husband Vulcan/Hepheastus on the other side of the divide. (There might be some issues between Athena and Hephaestus after that whole rape thing too...)<br /> <br /> Roman sea power was of central importance and Neptune wasn't a non-entity by any means. Roman sea power was key to the strength and integrity (even the existence) of the Republic and then the Empire. Some of the greatest battles of Rome were naval battles (like 11 during the Punic Wars and then the Battle of Actium, which created the Empire, etc.). One of the biggest claims to fame of Pompey was defeating pirates that were plaguing Roman trade. An integral part of the Pax Romana was keeping the Mediterranean open for said trade. Neptune's temple may not have been on the forum, but it was on the Campus Martius, So, not inconsequential at all. And he had a much more significant cultic presence in the logical locations of the actual ports that served Rome (Cosa, Ostia). Mussolini may not have built up his navy, but Neptune would probably have a serious interest in having a new Empire controlling the sea. Much more than, say, Njord might.<br /> <br /> Minerva was nigh as important as Juno in Roman worship, but you put her on the other side, in fact LEADING the other side, so, while I like Juno where you put her, it's not like it's a lock. You've split the Capitoline Trio into it's constituent thirds. So Jupiter is off puttering around not taking sides, even though he's as, if not more important, to Rome than his wife. Juno was the guardian of Rome as polity sure, but she seems to have been relatively cool with whichever way the government swung, though the implications seem that she was more important to the Republic (vis-a-vis the Senate) than the Empire (vis-a-vis the Emperor). (Though, that is actually dipping out of mythology, Scion's source, into religion, which is, in Sun Tzu's parlance, &quot;dangerous ground&quot; when used as background for game-related decisions.)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I see the role of Dionysius in regards the mural (other than it's actual existence as a piece of art, but, even then, there are other deities who fit the bill as muses for such things). In any case, if that's enough to put him on the side of the Allies, why isn't Zeus? I mean, the whole eagle carrying thunderbolts as the national seal and all. That's a much bigger overall link than the mural. In fact, it's even in the mural. Plus, apparently his own son raising Hades out in the West. It just seems like Dionysious/Bacchus would be the proverbial fiddler while Rome was burning, either intrinsically or burning something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 02-27-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:26:03-08:00","id":838369,"title":"","content":"Zeus is ALWAYS neutral in mortal wars according to the Iliad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:55:54-08:00","id":838430,"title":"","content":"And yet, every Roman Legion marched behind Jupiter's eagle, for they, the Romans, held him higher than all other peoples and that was why he approved of their conquests....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:52:08-08:00","id":840690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=838430#post838430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, every Roman Legion marched behind Jupiter's eagle, for they, the Romans, held him higher than all other peoples and that was why he approved of their conquests....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you want to tell Jupiter (Zeus) that another God supersedes his authority, then be my guest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:13:56-08:00","id":840704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=840690#post840690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to tell Jupiter (Zeus) that another God supersedes his authority, then be my guest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand your post. No one's challenging Zeus's authority over the members of his pantheon, such as it is (since he doesn't really have complete control, as some of his family did things he didn't like and he didn't always smite them, just grumbled thunderously...)<br /> <br /> We were tossing around ideas for a different WWII with a divided Dodekatheon (literally, since it's the big 12 +2 that we're divvying up) and what role Zeus plays (and I'll just use Zeus for the sake of convenience, since Jupiter is just a Latin attempt to handle the Greek /z/ in a language that doesn't have it, e.g. &quot;Jupiter&quot; = &quot;Zeus Pater&quot; for someone that can't pronounce /z/ and substitutes /zh/, written as &quot;j&quot;).<br /> <br /> Glamour is holding forth the perspective from the Iliad were Zeus was the referee. He didn't play the game and he called it and forbid the gods to get directly involved when tempers were running too high. (It seemed more like he was calling it because he just didn't want to hear Ares and Aphrodite whining after Diomedes hurt them. Zeus as the god of &quot;don't bother me&quot;. Probably because he was eyeing someone's wife or daugther....<br /> <br /> I was offering as an alternative that the Roman version of the same dude DEFINITELY took sides. Specifically, as far as the Romans were concerned he took THEIR side. <br /> <br /> It's germane to the discussion because, if the Romans weren't delusional, that would definitely bend Zeus to the &quot;pro-Roman/pro-Axis&quot; side of the divide and might change the whole nature of it. In essence the &quot;not so loyal opposition&quot; might have to act somewhat clandestinely, possibly hoping that Athena's special place in her father's heart would protect them from the brunt of his Jovian wrath when he finds out about it. Or there might be some other way the whole thing could fall out. <br /> <br /> But there is a core and very salient point that Glamour has pointed out. The Allies are largely the product of the Athena-like principles among other things, and it's hard to see Italy's role in the Axis in having her (among others of her willfull family) abadnoning the things they care about in favor of a nation that doesn't seem to embody their particular personal principles. Even under the whatever of the new rules, it seems like getting your mantles yanked around into uncomfortable and binding ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T01:22:04-08:00","id":845522,"title":"","content":"So, with the idea of an American &quot;Pantheon&quot; as a growing Circle of Demigods under the sponsorship of Columbia (Athena), here are my initial picks...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Uncle Sam, Scion of Tyr and War of 1812 veteran; claims purview of Duty to Country<br /> <br /> Rosie the Riveter, Scion of Brighid, and New Dealer union worker and feminist, claims both industry and collective action<br /> <br /> Harriet Tubman, &quot;Scion&quot; (not by blood, one of the other origins) of Eshu Elegba (through a Christian lens), purview of liberation<br /> <br /> Pecos Bill, Scion of Zeus, claims domain of the frontier and the conquest of the wilderness, became the first &quot;Space Cowboy&quot; in the 1960s<br /> <br /> Bass Reeves, the Lone Ranger, Scion of Horus, dominion over justice<br /> <br /> Johnny Appleseed, Scion of Wikadjek (his first ever son by a white woman), dominion over the fertility of the land<br /> <br /> Bre'er Rabbit, literal offspring of Anansi and a Nunnehi (Cherokee Lesser Divinity), these days increasingly given to cartoonish pranks and repeating the lines &quot;eeeeeh, what's up doc?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's my initial list with no Pantheon crossover, other candidates include<br /> <br /> Marilyn Monroe, mortal deified through sacrifice to the cult of celebrity, now the emobidment of said cult - don't know what Pantheon/Patron-God to tie her too... I keep thinking Hathor<br /> <br /> Nikolai Tesla, need a technological innovation figure, and an immigrant at that - probably a blood son of Zeus (hence &quot;lightning&quot;) adopted by Hephaestus?<br /> <br /> Johnny Reb, the anti-federalist/jeffersonian/confederate counterpart to federalist/hamiltonian/unionist Uncle Sam. Also the primary carrier of the burden of the sin of slavery and jim crow in the Pantheon (though several of the others are less innocent in America's racial hierarchy than they'd like to pretend, Uncle Sam and Pecos Bill first and foremost)<br /> <br /> Captain Stormalong, Scion of Njord?, embodiment of American sea-power<br /> <br /> John Henry, not sure on patron/parentage, but he's a good example of someone whose Legend (rather than history) says they died, and thus is a potential reincarnation or claimed Legend PC option<br /> <br /> Amelia Earhart, I'm thinking recruited as a Valkyrie by Odin &amp; Freyja, but her desire to break new bounds led her to go rogue and fly American souls all over the cosmos to wherever they most belong...<br /> <br /> Paul Bunyan, I'm thinking son of the Finnish god Tapio? Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Then I'm thinking there should be some representative of corporate capitalism/consumerism (like a political cartoon robber baron?), and another who represents clandestine state power - either an mib, or some pyramid headed all-seeing Scion of Thoth...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-11-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T07:58:24-08:00","id":845637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Amelia Earhart, I'm thinking recruited as a Valkyrie by Odin &amp; Freyja, but her desire to break new bounds led her to go <span style=\"color:red\">rouge</span> and fly American souls all over the cosmos to wherever they most belong... </div> </div> </div>(word colored r<sup>og</sup>u<sub>e</sub> is personal pet peeve of mine.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-11-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T08:20:26-08:00","id":845648,"title":"","content":"sorry, fixed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:10:06-07:00","id":848180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=845522#post845522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I'm thinking there should be some representative of corporate capitalism/consumerism (like a political cartoon robber baron?), and another who represents clandestine state power - either an mib, or some pyramid headed all-seeing Scion of Thoth...</div> </div> </div> </div>For the consumerism one, how about the Animal Spirits? Twins, one bullish and one bearish. Possibly of Manitouk descent. For the clandestine state power one, what about Secret Agent John Courage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:38:30-07:00","id":849370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=845522#post845522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marilyn Monroe, mortal deified through sacrifice to the cult of celebrity, now the emobidment of said cult - don't know what Pantheon/Patron-God to tie her too... I keep thinking Hathor</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just &quot;Candle in the Wind&quot; playing in my head, but given the self-destructive bent celebrity culture can have, I'm really leaning towards something Greek; that seems more archetypically <i>them</i>, although others can feel free to correct me..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:26:09-07:00","id":849389,"title":"","content":"Marilyn had such a sad time of it, I personally want her to be a heroic figure, to make up for the garbage and petty snickering she faced on Earth in spite of her talent and skill. The woman was a great talent who achieved great skill, and she was treated like a smutty joke. Lets make her a dignified Goddess. Perhaps the goddess of Innocent Love and Vindication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T23:19:21-07:00","id":849621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=849389#post849389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marilyn had such a sad time of it, I personally want her to be a heroic figure, to make up for the garbage and petty snickering she faced on Earth in spite of her talent and skill. The woman was a great talent who achieved great skill, and she was treated like a smutty joke. Lets make her a dignified Goddess. Perhaps the goddess of Innocent Love and Vindication.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, then I'm more likely not to use her at all, because what I need is a distinctly American deity of media/cult of celebrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T09:54:45-07:00","id":849777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=849621#post849621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, then I'm more likely not to use her at all, because what I need is a distinctly American deity of media/cult of celebrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the two are mutually exclusive. The Cult of Celebrity also involves all the negatives of being famous. Loved and hated. Adored and picked apart. Cherished and despised. The later is like the shadow of the former. Meaning that it's lesser and related. No one cares about the pecadillos of those no one cares about, neh?<br /> <br /> Marilyn seems like a perfect fit for a goddess. She had a hero's journey from obscurity in nowhere, a transformation, a fall from grace. She was married to Joe Dimaggio, the most famous athlete, thereby joining the two sides of American celebrity, sports and entertainment. She had legendary (in all senses of the word) affairs with the greatest and most beloved political leader, Pres. Kennedy and the most famous scientist, Einstein.<br /> <br /> And her legend had legs (in both senses of the words).<br /> <br /> Who else COULD it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T03:20:25-07:00","id":850477,"title":"","content":"Ok I'm thinking Ishtar as the patron goddess of Marilyn's deification (we don't know how exactly the &quot;mortal made divine&quot; splat works yet, so we'll see).<br /> <br /> I also decided to make Johnny Reb a reincarnated deity, though he's not advertising his actual identity. He's the reborn Phoenician God Attar, the Morning Star. The ultimate divine rebel*<br /> <br /> *Rebels who win, like Zeus or the American Founding Fathers don't get defined in their Legend as Rebels. Defeat, ala the Morning Star and the Confederacy is a core component of that Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T15:27:29-07:00","id":920590,"title":"","content":"I think you're confusing Einstein with Arthur Miller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:53:20-07:00","id":947462,"title":"","content":"I'm super new tabletop rpg's since I only started playing a yr and a half ago, but Scion is for sure the game I am enjoying the most so far and my character is from the Yankee Pantheon. I agree that they are pretty awesome and a great way to introduce the idea of modern day Pantheons. I grew up listening to those characters stories and just always loved them so I jumped at the opportunity to create a Scion based on one of them. Of course, while I like all the characters in the Pantheon, I decided to try my hand at creating a new god for them based on Molly Pitcher and it's worked out extremely well so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12229-wondersteven","name":"WonderSteven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:28:50-07:00","id":949057,"title":"","content":"If people are retconning Paul Bunyan to be some sort of giant, then exactly how large would he be? According to the legends told about him, he dug out the Grand Canyon just by dragging his axe along the ground while he walked. Sounds like that would be a Legend 12 threat, right there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:10:26-07:00","id":950115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=949057#post949057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people are retconning Paul Bunyan to be some sort of giant, then exactly how large would he be? According to the legends told about him, he dug out the Grand Canyon just by dragging his axe along the ground while he walked. Sounds like that would be a Legend 12 threat, right there!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And his boot print created lakes. In our game that is still part of his story, but he is able to create an avatar of himself that is smaller to consort with humans. I'm actually introducing a Scion of Paul Bunyan that is a hipster with the lumberjack look who has a Rabbit that he dyes blue and calls it Blueberry. He's kind of embraced his heritage on an ironic level. Or so he says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12229-wondersteven","name":"WonderSteven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T11:59:23-07:00","id":950165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WonderSteven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950115#post950115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And his boot print created lakes. In our game that is still part of his story, but he is able to create an avatar of himself that is smaller to consort with humans. I'm actually introducing a Scion of Paul Bunyan that is a hipster with the lumberjack look who has a Rabbit that he dyes blue and calls it Blueberry. He's kind of embraced his heritage on an ironic level. Or so he says.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were Paul Bunyan, I would so want to step on this dude. Then Babe could eat the squished bits. A big blue ox has high protein requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:53:24-07:00","id":950453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950165#post950165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were Paul Bunyan, I would so want to step on this dude. Then Babe could eat the squished bits. A big blue ox has high protein requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haha I get that. We are taking him as the more jovial of the Yankees tho and has the belief that everyone carves their own unique path so he's kind of like blindly proud of his son. Haven't fully worked out the kinks yet, but that's what we are working around. A gay hipster Scion of Paul Bunyan living in NYC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12229-wondersteven","name":"WonderSteven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T06:46:08-07:00","id":950537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950165#post950165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were Paul Bunyan, I would so want to step on this dude. Then Babe could eat the squished bits. A big blue ox has high protein requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Babe is a typhonian, has to be.<br /> <br /> As for why she's blue...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T09:34:36-07:00","id":950593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950537#post950537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Babe is a typhonian, has to be.<br /> <br /> As for why she's blue...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of the winter of blue snow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:09:54-07:00","id":950708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950593#post950593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because of the winter of blue snow?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, I don't know what that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:25:02-07:00","id":950720,"title":"","content":"That's part of the &quot;mythology&quot; of Paul Bunyan. That's when he found Babe.<br /> <br /> Vide: <a href=\"http://www.loving2learn.com/SuperSubjects/ReadingandLanguage/FavoriteStories2/TallTales/TheStoryofPaulBunyan.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.loving2learn.com/SuperSub...aulBunyan.aspx</a><br /> <br /> That's pretty much the &quot;core cannon&quot; of the Paul Bunyan &quot;mythos&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:55:56-07:00","id":950732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950720#post950720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's part of the &quot;mythology&quot; of Paul Bunyan. That's when he found Babe.<br /> <br /> Vide: <a href=\"http://www.loving2learn.com/SuperSubjects/ReadingandLanguage/FavoriteStories2/TallTales/TheStoryofPaulBunyan.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.loving2learn.com/SuperSub...aulBunyan.aspx</a><br /> <br /> That's pretty much the &quot;core cannon&quot; of the Paul Bunyan &quot;mythos&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, well it's been over 10 years since I've heard / read any of this folk lore stuff. Was bound to forget most of it eventually. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:35:51-07:00","id":950867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950165#post950165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were Paul Bunyan, I would so want to step on this dude. Then Babe could eat the squished bits. A big blue ox has high protein requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I think Paul Bunyan would have a sense of humor, I can't imagine him, or any god-level mythic figure, being ok with one of their Scions \u200bchoosing a Path intended to openly mock a profession so intimately tied to their own Legend. The reason nobody likes hipsters is that their so-called &quot;irony&quot; is nothing more than obnoxious mockery, devoid of any sincerity or integrity.<br /> <br /> Forging your own destiny is one thing, insulting your Divine Parent's core concept is another: Scions of Aphrodite <b><u><span style=\"color:#b22222\">DO NOT</span></u></b> take vows of celibacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:43:08-07:00","id":950873,"title":"","content":"Paul Bunyan's deeds actually seem more like those of a Titan in many cases. (Whoops! I made the Great Lakes!, Etc.) And a lot of his &quot;adventures&quot; seem to deal with narrowly avoiding the consequences of his size and/or appetite. He might seem like a nice guy... but a nice who has a dark side and that side is something you never, ever, want to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:26:51-07:00","id":950906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950867#post950867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as I think Paul Bunyan would have a sense of humor, I can't imagine him, or any god-level mythic figure, being ok with one of their Scions \u200bchoosing a Path intended to openly mock a profession so intimately tied to their own Legend. The reason nobody likes hipsters is that their so-called &quot;irony&quot; is nothing more than obnoxious mockery, devoid of any sincerity or integrity.<br /> <br /> Forging your own destiny is one thing, insulting your Divine Parent's core concept is another: Scions of Aphrodite <b><u><span style=\"color:#b22222\">DO NOT</span></u></b> take vows of celibacy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=950873#post950873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paul Bunyan's deeds actually seem more like those of a Titan in many cases. (Whoops! I made the Great Lakes!, Etc.) And a lot of his &quot;adventures&quot; seem to deal with narrowly avoiding the consequences of his size and/or appetite. He might seem like a nice guy... but a nice who has a dark side and that side is something you never, ever, want to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, I can see where you are coming from and I respect your opinion. While we are taking a more subjective approach to his story, his Scion is in his own way respectful of his Divine Parent/Lineage, but at first he's not as open about it as he could be. I specifically worded how he embraces his heritage the way he does because his journey is more about self discovery. He Eventually, he's going to realize that it wasn't ironic at all. That he actually wants to be who he has fashioned himself after and become an active role in the Yankee Scion Band we are building. His road to self discovery is about ownership and pride.<br /> <br /> Of course, although I'm creating the characters with the GM, I am open to some ideas and suggestions as well. We were toying with actually making the bunny (or other animal) one of his gifts he gets from Paul.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12229-wondersteven","name":"WonderSteven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T09:26:34-07:00","id":951158,"title":"","content":"It's your character and your game. Honestly, this conversation has made me more amenable to Scion-&quot;Tall Tales&quot; (as opposed to the standard Scion -&quot;Mythic Cycle&quot;) than I ever have been before.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Paul would think the &quot;Slacker-jack&quot; was a great joke. He has a great big sense of humor. But,if/when he found out that his son was just being &quot;ironic&quot; about it and didn't take any aspect of his father's legend seriously.... there would be problems on a Paul Bunyan-level scale. (The idea of Paul Bunyan punching a slacker through the Rocky Mountains and creating the Great Tunnel of Colorado or the &quot;Man-Shaped Splatter&quot; on the Moon, or all the way across Canada and embedding him head-first like a flag at the North Pole seems entirely appropriate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T10:50:33-07:00","id":951201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=951158#post951158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's your character and your game. Honestly, this conversation has made me more amenable to Scion-&quot;Tall Tales&quot; (as opposed to the standard Scion -&quot;Mythic Cycle&quot;) than I ever have been before.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Paul would think the &quot;Slacker-jack&quot; was a great joke. He has a great big sense of humor. But,if/when he found out that his son was just being &quot;ironic&quot; about it and didn't take any aspect of his father's legend seriously.... there would be problems on a Paul Bunyan-level scale. (The idea of Paul Bunyan punching a slacker through the Rocky Mountains and creating the Great Tunnel of Colorado or the &quot;Man-Shaped Splatter&quot; on the Moon, or all the way across Canada and embedding him head-first like a flag at the North Pole seems entirely appropriate).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of the best parts about tall tales is how the characters seem to give the middle finger to logic and go over the top when accomplishing a goal.<br /> <br /> Like Pecos Bill...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Well, seems Texas is having a drought. Guess I'll ride three states over and lasso the rain clouds from California!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I think playing a folktale Scion can be just as fun (if not more so) as playing a mythic Scion, if you don't mind a bit of silliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-15-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:18:59-07:00","id":951214,"title":"","content":"And a little more comprehensive dig to try to get some actual parents.... <br /> <br /> They need to have some Tall Tales associated. So, Uncle Sam - no, Columbia -no. <br /> <br /> With, probably, a way for mortals to &quot;ascend&quot; to appropriate status... Johnny Appleseed - yes, but that would also include Daniel Boone, George Washington, Davey Crocket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:25:33-07:00","id":951217,"title":"","content":"Meh, I wouldn't really say George Washington goes on the list. Benjamin Franklin, though... Not only did he harness the power of electricity, but he was apparently quite the sex fiend. Sounds an awful lot like Zeus!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:03:08-07:00","id":951228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=951217#post951217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, I wouldn't really say George Washington goes on the list. Benjamin Franklin, though... Not only did he harness the power of electricity, but he was apparently quite the sex fiend. Sounds an awful lot like Zeus!</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is not HISTORY, but LEGEND and Ben Franklin has a ton of history, but he's about tied with the George Washington as far as legends go.... Ben Franklin with his lightning kite. George and his honest cherry tree chopping... Both are much more legendary than, say, Betsy Ross, (though she as at least one legend) with nothing else and not much history to add on. <br /> <br /> Maybe the &quot;ascended mortals&quot; are more of a demigod-level in a Tall Tales game. <br /> <br /> What I'd REALLY want to see is more like Paul Bunyan (who had a whole slew of other lesser tall tale types associated with him) and Pecos Bill. Figures like Mink Fink, King of the River or Stormalong from the East Coast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:35:42-07:00","id":951657,"title":"","content":"I always liked the aspect of their living embodiments of Ideals that the nation subscribe to and the fairytale aspect just being a convenient way to express it. I like the nation embodiment gods like Britannia, Rodina Mat and so on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:31:01-07:00","id":951777,"title":"","content":"I've started tinkering with the idea that several great presidents may have been Avatars or Incarnations of Uncle Sam. Certainly, there is a bit of Abraham Lincoln in his most iconic depiction.<br /> \u200bColumbia...while there really are no tales(tall or otherwise) about her, I dig the idea of an ascended Scion of Athena as Goddess of Democracy.<br /> Really only the one story about John Henry, but I really love that story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:50:23-07:00","id":951788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=951657#post951657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked the aspect of their living embodiments of Ideals that the nation subscribe to and the fairytale aspect just being a convenient way to express it. I like the nation embodiment gods like Britannia, Rodina Mat and so on</div> </div> </div> </div>But, what are their STORIES? What Legend do they have? It's like trying to use evidence of cultic activity to set up gods in Scion. Ultimately fruitless. Scion is a game about myths not religion. Scion Tall Tales would be about stories not.... what?... artistic depiction?<br /> <br /> Columbia, Uncle Sam, Rodina Mat, Britannia... what stories can you tell me about them? What did they do? Is Columbia Uncle Sam's wife? Mother? Did Columbia come to Christopher Columbus in a vision and guide him to Hispaniola? (If she did.... what a bitch.... totally culpable for mass ethnocide). Did Uncle Sam fight in WWII? If so, what did he do? If you want to use them, you're going to have to make such stories up. Which goes into the same category as &quot;made-up pantheons&quot;. Fine, if you like them, but, ultimately they are going to be tissue-paper thin compared to the depth and richness of more robust legends. Hells, what are the Fatebindings on such paper doll Legends? I can see what expectations people would have of Paul Bunyan, but what do people expect from Columbia?<br /> <br /> I can find a wealth of Paul Bunyan stories pretty easily. There are similar sets of stories out there for Mike Fink, Pecos Bill, Stormalong, Then there are the &quot;one-story wonders&quot; like Betsy Ross, Johnny Appleseed, John Henry, etc (most of whom are partially historic, thereby opening the way for Ben Franklin, George Washington... Teddy Roosevelt?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:33:42-07:00","id":951821,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn thinking the Yankee GodRealm should it be modeled after Washington DC? <br /> <br /> hopefully without being accosted by homeless people (Like I was only time I went there)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:03:25-07:00","id":951896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=951821#post951821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmn thinking the Yankee GodRealm should it be modeled after Washington DC?<br /> <br /> hopefully without being accosted by homeless people (Like I was only time I went there)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally envision it to be a representation of the industrial revolution, seeing as how their purview was literally based on industry. Guarded by steampunk Colossi, Tesla Coils, and other marvels of human ingenuity. (Given a legendary spin to them)<br /> <br /> <br /> And within the heart of this realm is Nikola Tesla's legendary free power generator, providing clean, sufficient energy to the whole pantheon!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=951788#post951788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Uncle Sam fight in WWII? If so, what did he do?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uncle Sam was a butcher who was said to feed the troops during the war...<br /> <br /> Then he somehow became a national icon who wants everybody to join his army!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-16-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:30:12-07:00","id":951919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=951228#post951228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is not HISTORY, but LEGEND and Ben Franklin has a ton of history, but he's about tied with the George Washington as far as legends go.... Ben Franklin with his lightning kite. George and his honest cherry tree chopping... Both are much more legendary than, say, Betsy Ross, (though she as at least one legend) with nothing else and not much history to add on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, now that I think about it, I believe history is exactly the problem here.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a pantheon, you have to remember that the Yankees are, in fact, quite new. They've been around for less than 600 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember that when it comes to story telling, they often grow over time, becoming more grandiose and ridiculous with each generation. You can rationalize it by saying that in time, they will grow to match the stories of the more ancient religions, but their accomplishments are still relatively new, and we have more reliable methods of keeping recorded history safe than we did in the time of ancient Greece, or Egypt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:24:42-07:00","id":951966,"title":"","content":"everyone want to work on the godrealm and individual realms see how it looks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:13:50-07:00","id":952017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=951919#post951919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, now that I think about it, I believe history is exactly the problem here.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a pantheon, you have to remember that the Yankees are, in fact, quite new. They've been around for less than 600 years.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember that when it comes to story telling, they often grow over time, becoming more grandiose and ridiculous with each generation. You can rationalize it by saying that in time, they will grow to match the stories of the more ancient religions, but their accomplishments are still relatively new, and we have more reliable methods of keeping recorded history safe than we did in the time of ancient Greece, or Egypt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, this is not a game about what legends may form or accrete around historical figures or fabulous creations over time. In Scion, those stories are real in a very important way. They happened. I can't see how to set up a game today around the the myths that will someday form around a figure but haven't done so yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:28:56-07:00","id":952028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=952017#post952017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, this is not a game about what legends may form or accrete around historical figures or fabulous creations over time. In Scion, those stories are real in a very important way. They happened. I can't see how to set up a game today around the the myths that will someday form around a figure but haven't done so yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that something we have to remember about the game is that it is all about creativity. Nyrufa is right, those stories grew and evolved over time, so in your specific game, how did they evolve It's up to you as the storyteller to add something. It's up to the players to come up with something. The newer Pantheons are so intriguing to me because there is so much room for creativity and artistic freedom when it comes to coming up with a story for not just the player character, but the actual gods that created them. We get to shape them ourselves and make them whatever we want them to be and whatever we want them to represent in this modern age. It's the freaking American Dream over here... *I say to myself in a NY accent*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12229-wondersteven","name":"WonderSteven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:57:26-07:00","id":952052,"title":"","content":"Johnny appleseed probaly has (Duh) an apple grove for his realm, likely displaying the theme of peaceful cooexistence<br /> <br /> Is it stupid to have a church inside a go realm? as thats part of his legend being a missionary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:11:22-07:00","id":952061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=952052#post952052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Johnny appleseed probaly has (Duh) an apple grove for his realm, likely displaying the theme of peaceful cooexistence<br /> <br /> Is it stupid to have a church inside a go realm? as thats part of his legend being a missionary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Amatsukami have at least one Buddhist shrine in their Godrealm, even though they're the Gods of Shinto, so I don't see a problem with it. Other than the whole monotheism idea in what is clearly a polytheistic pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:35:36-07:00","id":952160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WonderSteven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=952028#post952028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that something we have to remember about the game is that it is all about creativity. Nyrufa is right, those stories grew and evolved over time, so in your specific game, how did they evolve It's up to you as the storyteller to add something. It's up to the players to come up with something. The newer Pantheons are so intriguing to me because there is so much room for creativity and artistic freedom when it comes to coming up with a story for not just the player character, but the actual gods that created them. We get to shape them ourselves and make them whatever we want them to be and whatever we want them to represent in this modern age. It's the freaking American Dream over here... *I say to myself in a NY accent*</div> </div> </div> </div>The game isn't all about creativity. There really isn't a game out there about that. I did play one once where the players essentially created a universe from the ground up as the gods. That was about as purely creative as I've seen it ever get. Even then it was constrained with concepts like &quot;gods&quot;, &quot;creation&quot; &amp; &quot;universe&quot;.<br /> <br /> This game is about a specific setting with a specific type of character. The setting is a world where myths, legends and/or folklore are factually true. It's the core conceit from which all others follow. The following conceit is that the player characters are connected (almost always genetically) with the figures of said myths, legends or folklore. Coming up with stories about the gods (or whatever Paul Bunyan is) is all well and good. Adding to or embroidering the story. But coming up with everything from the ground up and you start loosing the point of this game vis-a-vis others.<br /> <br /> Your slacker-jack son of Paul Bunyan with his faux lumberjack chique, his man bun and his blue bunny is a perfect example of a Scion Tall Tales character. He riffs off the lore of his father. You've set up room for conflict and for resolution. Everything makes sense and is immediately reconizable.<br /> <br /> If I was to make up a Scion Tall Tales character who was a sous chef at a high end bistro, who is the son of Sloppy Jane the Best-est School Cafeteria Lunch Lady.... well, it's kinda funny, but even if I add in that he has a small carton of milk that never empties and has prophetic pictures of the next victim the band will save, or a super special hair net that he absolutely HATES, but, when worn makes him so intimidating that a diner will be intimidating anything he serves them, this dude isn't really on the level of Paul Bunyan's son and never will be. In fact, he is closer to the &quot;joke Scions&quot; from the April Fool's Day Scion supplement. <br /> <br /> That character is a little extreme, but it's a sort of reverse &quot;proof of context&quot;. A character that's generated out a set of legends that are created out of whole cloth is going to lack resonance with the game being played. Even if a player is willing to go balls to the wall and write up a myth cycle for their fictive legendary parent, it's still going to feel pretty hollow compared to the slackerjack or the weatherman son of Pecos Bill, the civil rights lawyer daughter of Brer Rabbit, Mike Fink's Bayou-based Army Corps of Engineer son, or even the fashionista daughter of Betsy Ross (and the last one is pretty weak as it is, considering Betsy's legend and the history involved...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T20:27:49-07:00","id":952249,"title":"","content":"Being a Scion does not mean you're bound to follow in your divine parent's footsteps, though. It just means you're predisposed to having the same characteristics / skills as them. And even then, that's not strictly guaranteed to happen.<br /> <br /> Remember, Scion isn't about reenacting the legends of the past, it's about building your own legend. You are leaving your own mark on history as you become a legitimate member of your pantheon. Or, if you so desire, you can abandon your pantheon to go create your own.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the game does involve a lot of creative elements to it.<br /> <br /> And as for the myths being true, remember that in first edition of the game, the power of belief has a very real effect on the Gods. That's why they chose to retreat from the world in the first place, because they were afraid mortals would twist their legends to a point where it's unrecognizable.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, it makes perfect sense that the Yankee's legends would grow more impressive over time. In fact, it's already happened.<br /> <br /> Legends say that Washington was a great general who lead America to victory over the British. But historically, Washington was a pretty bad strategist and many of his victories were due to his experience as a farmer. He knew about the terrain and the weather, while the British army was not experienced for such things. In other words, the first president won the war through dumb luck!<br /> <br /> <br /> To the American people, the founding fathers were great men of intellect who fought for the equal rights of all. But historically, at least half of them were slave owners (including Washington) and objectified women. Their idea of democracy was also vastly different to what we have in place now.<br /> <br /> <br /> To reiterate my point: Legends, much like Tall Tales, grow over time, often becoming more impressive with each new generation. The Yankees aren't impressive now because they are so young. But given time, their believers will continue to build them up into something worthy of competing with the other pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-17-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T22:02:53-07:00","id":952305,"title":"","content":"Here's some stories about <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/uncle-sam/4005-3625/\" target=\"_blank\">Uncle Sam.</a> Admittedly, only from the past century, but what can you do? <b>Tales grow in the telling.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:37:21-07:00","id":952932,"title":"","content":"oh it said Uncle sam was ELECTED to his position as head of the pantheon, would another election be a bad thing to RP, with either hmmmn cant think of anyone... maybe johnny appleseed, or preferably a PC running against him...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T20:37:52-07:00","id":952957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=952932#post952932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh it said Uncle sam was ELECTED to his position as head of the pantheon, would another election be a bad thing to RP, with either hmmmn cant think of anyone... maybe johnny appleseed, or preferably a PC running against him...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't remember if one of the books suggested it, or if it was a story hook somewhere on the forums, but a replacement election can be a thing if you want to do it that way. Although the question becomes how long is an immortal president allowed to serve their term?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:51:23-07:00","id":953115,"title":"","content":"Maybe not that long, but they never ratified the 22nd ammendment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:40:52-07:00","id":953201,"title":"","content":"maybe indefinitely or they never passed the 22nd ammendment themselves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T08:44:39-07:00","id":953204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=952957#post952957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can't remember if one of the books suggested it, or if it was a story hook somewhere on the forums, but a replacement election can be a thing if you want to do it that way. Although the question becomes how long is an immortal president allowed to serve their term?</div> </div> </div> </div>If ,and only if, you think that the &quot;Spirit of America&quot; adheres to the Constitution and you haven't creatively licensed away the actual US Constitution:<br /> <br /> 8 years. XXII Amendment. Ratified Feb. 27, 1851<br /> <br /> Possibly, with a VERY permissive reading:<br /> President for 8 years,<br /> Elected Vice President, 3rd year+1 day becomes President for remainder of term<br /> Elected President for 4 years<br /> So 13 year +364 days (less permissive, take off the the last for 11 years + 364 days)<br /> <br /> If you want to go completely crazy:<br /> Above +<br /> Elected Vice-President, President steps down after being inaugurated, Seves as President for remainder of term<br /> AGAIN Elected Vice-President, etc.<br /> and so on<br /> <br /> After that you have to start digging deep into the XX Amendment (Ratified Jan. 23, 1933), then there are more options. Or start amending the Constitution with all that entails (4 different ways to do that) Constitution proper Article V.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of other options that spin off of the above, but they are minor adjustments.<br /> <br /> So, if he is a sort of permanent President, who are his shills to stand for President when he's Vice-President/President-in-Waiting?<br /> <br /> And is any of that legal two-stepping very &quot;American&quot; in the way Uncle Sam is supposed to present it? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:03:17-07:00","id":953415,"title":"","content":"oh think Senior yankee gods would still create mini nukes, in modern times as their power, or back in the revolutionary or civil war?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:32:40-07:00","id":953554,"title":"","content":"My take has been that they measure time a little differently, being immortal: 1 century of our time = 1 year of theirs. If Sam's administration began with the start of our independence, then he's still on his first term in office.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:07:34-07:00","id":953569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=953554#post953554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take has been that they measure time a little differently, being immortal: 1 century of our time = 1 year of theirs. If Sam's administration began with the start of our independence, then he's still on his first term in office.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would make sense, especially if they go by the two term maximum rule. But Uncle Sam wasn't even a national symbol until WW2. So how could he have been elected at the founding of America?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:25:33-07:00","id":953581,"title":"","content":"Because he's George Washington and his first term begins after he ascends to Uncle Sam-hood, probably after some transitional demigod phase where he was a yankee-doodle dandy....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T22:18:55-07:00","id":953673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=953569#post953569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would make sense, especially if they go by the two term maximum rule. But Uncle Sam wasn't even a national symbol until WW2. So how could he have been elected at the founding of America?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUncle Sam goes back at least as far as the war of 1812, when American soldiers received crates of meat stamped &quot;U.S.&quot;. The butcher supplying them was named Sam Wilson. I've been going with the idea that Sam is an ascended Scion of King Arthur, or someone else connected to the British monarchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:29:45-07:00","id":953827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=953673#post953673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bUncle Sam goes back at least as far as the war of 1812, when American soldiers received crates of meat stamped &quot;U.S.&quot;. The butcher supplying them was named Sam Wilson. I've been going with the idea that Sam is an ascended Scion of King Arthur, or someone else connected to the British monarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I knew he was a butcher, but I thought that happened in WW2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyways, we need an Arthurian pantheon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T10:11:12-07:00","id":953899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=953827#post953827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I knew he was a butcher, but I thought that happened in WW2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyways, we need an Arthurian pantheon!</div> </div> </div> </div>There has got to be a better word for that than &quot;pantheon&quot;, because, it's NOT a pantheon, which, by definition is a group of gods. And the Arthurian Knights aren't gods and never have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T14:50:55-07:00","id":954050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=953899#post953899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There has got to be a better word for that than &quot;pantheon&quot;, because, it's NOT a pantheon, which, by definition is a group of gods. And the Arthurian Knights aren't gods and never have been.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well same could be said for the Yankees. They were folk heroes, or spirits of the American dream, not divine beings. The one exception being Bre'er Rabbit, since he's also known as Coyote, who was a native American deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:27:30-07:00","id":954436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954050#post954050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well same could be said for the Yankees. They were folk heroes, or spirits of the American dream, not divine beings. The one exception being Bre'er Rabbit, since he's also known as Coyote, who was a native American deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Tall Tales-FolkTales are not a pantheon either. In fact, they aren't even a mythology. There are no shared stories. Paul Bunyan and Pecos Bill never team up. Uncle Sam doesn't give John Henry a pep-talk before the contest.<br /> <br /> Bre'r Rabbit may be based very loosely on the antics of an amalgam of several &quot;Rabbit&quot; gods that were shared by some tribes of the Eastern Coast of North America, but Bre'r Rabbit was never, ever, ever any &quot;Coyote&quot; god, no matter what the Scion Companions says. Period. That's <i><b>at best</b></i> <u>extremely</u> disrespectful to Native American Beliefs. For the sake of comparison, think the Gypsies book or autistic people being sources of overwhelming Banality. That bad. It's disrespectful the tribes from which the Bre'r Rabbit stories were (very loosely) derived and it's massively disrespectful to the over twenty different &quot;Coyote&quot; mythological figures in over a dozen tribes in about five different culture areas. The balance, but by no means all, adhere at least somewhat to a modernist Trickster archetype. Some aren't Tricksters at all. As far as comparative mythology goes, it would be worse than saying &quot;There's just an Indo-European Pantheon and one of the gods is 'Thunder-Man'. Any differences between Zeus, Jupiter, Thor, Perun (Slavic), Indra, Taranis (Gaelic) Teshub (Hittite), Tarhunt (Hurrian), Tishtriya (Persian), etc. are irrelevant. They are all one dude who just got around a lot and acted way different in different places. In fact, you should probably add in Baal Hadad (Canaanite), Tengri (Turkic) and Ukko (Finnish) in there as well, cultures that had next to nothing to do with Indo-Europeans, to make it as insensitive to actual differences in the various deities being lumped together as the concept of a &quot;Coyote&quot; god in a &quot;Native American&quot; pantheon is. The only analogy I can think of that encompasses adding &quot;Coyote&quot; to Bre'r Rabbit might be something like saying, &quot;Oh yeah, and there's no Set/Sutekh either. He's just Thunder-Man too&quot;. No. Just... No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:52:49-07:00","id":954454,"title":"","content":"Ah, I suppose that's why we haven't seen a Native American pantheon, then. They weren't a unified religion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> So in other words, the Yankees (name still doesn't feel right) and the Allied, were just a hashed together grab bag of popular figures to justify a World War 2 scenario.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, one of the Native American tribes helped out during the war, if I remember my history correctly. Using their native language as a form of coded message over the radio, so that right there is a good explanation for why their pantheon might be involved during WW2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:31:14-07:00","id":954480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954454#post954454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I suppose that's why we haven't seen a Native American pantheon, then. They weren't a unified religion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The best way to think about it is think of how small Europe is, and how many Pantheons it has. Then, how massive North America is. There are an absolute ton of viable Pantheons in North America, who are all different from each other and the like. The Animal Council of the Wyandot for example is fundamentally different from what you would find if you looked to some of the various Inuit Bands up north.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, a thing on the Unified religion bit. It's not that they were not a unified religion, it's that they were fundamentally different groups of people. The Tuatha, for example, are a non-unified religion. The Native North Americans had <i>different</i> religions, fundamentally, to each other. Modern media presents there as being things such as 'Native American Gods', but that's like saying, 'Asian God' which encompases the Shen, Deva, the Slavs depending on the century, the Kami, the Mongolian Pantheon, the Anunnaki, the Arabian Pantheon, the Cannanites, ect. These groups were different culturally from each other, it's not that they were not unified, it's that they were different peoples with different beliefs, customs, traditions, philosophies, everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954454#post954454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, one of the Native American tribes helped out during the war, if I remember my history correctly. Using their native language as a form of coded message over the radio, so that right there is a good explanation for why their pantheon might be involved during WW2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not great at American or World War History, but I believe it was Navajo. I know very little of Navajo history or their Pantheon, but I don't think they have had the best relationship with the United States Government. A lot of the Pantheon's predisposition to things, the people's relationship to the US government, and the like could be weighed to see if they'd be interested in participating in the World War scenario. (For example, if they are extreme isolationists like some Pantheons, it wouldn't make sense for them to get involved in the situation)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-20-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T18:13:18-07:00","id":954713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954480#post954480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not great at American or World War History, but I believe it was Navajo. I know very little of Navajo history or their Pantheon, but I don't think they have had the best relationship with the United States Government. A lot of the Pantheon's predisposition to things, the people's relationship to the US government, and the like could be weighed to see if they'd be interested in participating in the World War scenario. (For example, if they are extreme isolationists like some Pantheons, it wouldn't make sense for them to get involved in the situation)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Navajo. The Code Talkers. Best way to create a nigh unbreakable code. Just use a completely unknown language when communicating over the radio.<br /> <br /> No Native American tribe has had an unsullied relationship with the U.S. government, but the Navajo have managed to get through the apocalyptic invasion and subjugation doing ever so slightly better than most. Not great. Their situation vis-a-vis water is absolutely appalling. But they have a significant chunk of New Mexico, etc. as their semi-sovereign territory. And it's actually part of the lands they lived in pre-Contact. You could actually carve out Navajo Territory as a full-on state sized territory of its own (a la Nunavut). One could definitely say that, culturally, the Navajo are more culturally intact than, say, the Aztec. Well, than the Norse, Greek, etc. pantheons as well. <br /> <br /> I never did mock up a Navajo Pantheon. I had a Hopi/Pueblo Pantheon made up for one game to mess with the Scions by throwing them into situations that were completely beyond their ken. There was a bit of dabbling with the Navajo, but I decided not to split my efforts. Especially once I found out about Oraibi, an actual Pueblo town that has successfully resisted acculturation to use as a base for some Qatsina Scions and a place to meet a Hopi goddess. Hahti Wuti, effectively &quot;Grandmother Spider&quot;. <br /> <br /> As to whether the Navajo Pantheon (Diyin Dine'e?) would be part of the &quot;Allies&quot; during WWII... I think there's a bit of apples and oranges going on. The Allied &quot;Pantheons&quot; are loose amalgams of folk heroes and tall tales vs. Axis mythological pantheons (Greek/Roman, Japanese, Norse). So I'm not sure. If there were &quot;Allied&quot; pantheons that were equivalent in stature to the Allies (not sure who those would be), I could see some kind of agreement with Estsanatlehi, the sky goddess, or her sons (who are <i>really </i>like the Mayan Hero Twins) for a sort of mutually beneficial &quot;loan&quot;. To the Navajo, letting someone else use their language would seem to be a big deal. Their creation myth has a key role for the personification of speech (Bikeh Hozho). So I'm wondering what the Navajo got for their efforts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:32:29-07:00","id":954807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954454#post954454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, one of the Native American tribes helped out during the war, if I remember my history correctly. Using their native language as a form of coded message over the radio, so that right there is a good explanation for why their pantheon might be involved during WW2.</div> </div> </div> </div>They made a movie about it:<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0245562/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Windtalkers</i></a>. \u200bAlso, Navajo is NOT the correct name, that's actually Anasazi for &quot;enemy&quot;. The correct name is <a href=\"http://navajopeople.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Din\u00e9</b></a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:37:09-07:00","id":954825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954807#post954807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They made a movie about it:<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0245562/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Windtalkers</i></a>. \u200bAlso, Navajo is NOT the correct name, that's actually Anasazi for &quot;enemy&quot;. The correct name is <a href=\"http://navajopeople.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Din\u00e9</b></a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thanks for that! I will make note of that. I was so disappointed in my school system when I learned that Huron is not the actual name of the cultural group, and was pretty much just made up by Samuel de Champlain. Would have hoped they would have gone through and made sure they were teaching the correct names after they moved to properly using Inuit. Took a few months to drill Wyandot into my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T05:15:22-07:00","id":954909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954825#post954825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, thanks for that! I will make note of that. I was so disappointed in my school system when I learned that Huron is not the actual name of the cultural group, and was pretty much just made up by Samuel de Champlain. Would have hoped they would have gone through and made sure they were teaching the correct names after they moved to properly using Inuit. Took a few months to drill Wyandot into my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGlad I could help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:54:50-07:00","id":954999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/679302-the-yankee-and-the-allied-pantheons?p=954807#post954807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They made a movie about it:<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0245562/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Windtalkers</i></a>. \u200bAlso, Navajo is NOT the correct name, that's actually Anasazi for &quot;enemy&quot;. The correct name is <a href=\"http://navajopeople.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Din\u00e9</b></a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Navajo is the correct name in several important venues. For example, the US treaties are with the &quot;Navajo Indians&quot;, not the &quot;Dine Native Americans&quot;. Changing the appellation could (and has, for other tribes and nations and villages and communities) confused the issues (like land ownership, government assistance) in a very very bad way for the Native American group involved. Leadership in several tribes I worked with at one point were very definite on this point. So it's something that is very much a matter that has to be addressed on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that the name &quot;Navajo&quot; isn't a pejorative term from nearby culture (like &quot;Sioux&quot; aka &quot;those untrustworthy snakes&quot; for the Lakota or &quot;Eskimo&quot; aka &quot;raw fish eaters&quot; for the Inuit). It's a Tewa word that means &quot;Those guys from the wide valley&quot;. <br /> <br /> &quot;Dine&quot; as the Navajo name for themselves is correct but not dispositive. It, or a very close variant, is the word for &quot;people&quot; in most Na-Dene languages, which includes a number of cultural groups from the US Southwest including, but by no means limited to the Navajo. It also includes many tribes in British Columbia, Yukon and Alaska as well. The Navajo call themselves either Dine or Naabeeho. The Navajo Nation, in Navajo, is Naabeeho Binahasdzo.<br /> <br /> Anasazi is a world IN Navajo meaning &quot;Ancestors of our Enemies&quot; or &quot;Ancestral Enemies&quot; referring to the Ancestral Pueblo cultural ruins in Navajo Territory. The Anasazi aren't the ancestors of the Navajo. The Anasazi were the ancestors of the Pueblo tribes, including the Hopi and Zuni. We don't have any Anasazi words as the culture was effectively gone (well... moved) by 1350 AD. The languages of the Pueblo tribes are almost certainly descended from whatever the Anasazi spoke.<br /> <br /> The Anasazi are the &quot;bad guys&quot; in some Navajo myths and legends. A mythical vanished people who fell from grace, were sorcerers, etc. etc. Which might have some back-up archaeologically. Some of the Anasazi practices seems to have been the sorts of things that many other cultures find troublesome. In a sort of the same ways the later Aztecs squick people out. (And they were in contact with Mesoamerican cultures with those kind of customs... evidence of chocolate and macaw feathers that were imported from Central America have been found. But so were boiled and gnawed-on human bones...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 08-21-2016, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}